  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Existing evidence shows multiprofile scVI RNA is strong (~0.65 accuracy), while the only image-only test, ResNet50, is weak (~0.21). This leaves important uncertainty about whether the image modality can be useful at all or whether the weak result is due to a poor image encoder. config_013 tests a stronger pretrained image representation, ImageNet ViT-L, under the same simple image-only/single-profile setting, directly comparing to config_010. This is the best next experiment because it isolates image representation without changing profile setting, aggregation, or fusion, reducing uncertainty before spending budget on more complex multimodal fusion. If ViT-L improves image-only performance, it motivates multimodal ViT-L experiments; if not, it supports focusing on RNA-only multiprofile designs."
}

